{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The resource-server half of DPoP: given the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DPoP"},{"type":"text","text":" header a caller presented, decide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether it proves possession for "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" request and "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" access token, and return"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the key thumbprint that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator\/verifyTokenBinding(_:proofs:)"},{"type":"text","text":" then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matches against the token’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cnf.jkt"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Why this lives in the SDK","anchor":"Why-this-lives-in-the-SDK","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§21.7.2 is a ten-check list, and the contract is blunt about partial implementations:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"“Partial verification is worse than none, because it produces a guard that reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"success.”","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Nine of the ten look optional until someone builds an attack out of the one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that was skipped, so they belong in one audited place rather than in every application"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guarding an endpoint."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two most often missing: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"typ"},{"type":"text","text":" — without pinning it to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dpop+jwt"},{"type":"text","text":", any "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"other"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" JWT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signed by the same key (an access token, an ID token) is replayable as a proof; and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ath"},{"type":"text","text":" — without it, a proof captured on one request can be re-aimed at a different token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"held by the same key."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The algorithm comes from the key, never from the header","anchor":"The-algorithm-comes-from-the-key-never-from-the-header","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alg: none"},{"text":" and RSA-public-key-as-HMAC-secret are the same bug wearing different clothes:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"the token told the verifier how to check the token","type":"text"}]},{"text":". This enum dispatches on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"embedded key’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kty"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"crv"},{"text":", so an HMAC path is never reachable no matter what the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"header says.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/Request"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/